  "title": "Cessna 310 R — Normal Operating Procedures",
  "description": "Normal operating procedures for the Cessna 310 R light twin with Continental TSIO-520 turbocharged engines, constant-speed propellers, and retractable tricycle gear. Covers external walk-around through shutdown and securing. All airspeeds, power settings, fuel quantities, manifold pressure limits, temperature limits, and performance data must come from the specific aircraft POH. Both turbocharged engines require careful warm-up before takeoff. Fuel selector positions (main/aux tanks) are operationally important — verify against the specific aircraft. Retractable gear requires a positive gear check on every approach. Single-engine performance and Vmc awareness are essential for all phases of flight. Not a substitute for qualified multi-engine instruction or type-specific training.",
